From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 12/13] Plutonium: Wayland protocols

Protocols apps expect from a desktop: zwp_text_input_v3, xdg_activation_v1, wp_cursor_shape_v1, ext_idle_notify_v1, ext_data_control_v1, and server-side decorations.

It holds these changes:
- zwp_text_input_v3 in Exo, for GTK 4, Qt 6 and foot
- xdg_activation_v1, apps raise their windows through the shell
- wp_cursor_shape_v1, cursors by name for GTK 4, Qt 6 and foot
- ext_idle_notify_v1, apps hear when the user is idle
- ext_data_control_v1, the clipboard for clipboard managers

and the parts in these files of:
- Exo embedding (Phase 1) and window broker (Phase 2)
- agent keyboard focus beside the user's; the compositor decorates every window
- ext-image-copy-capture-v1 in Exo, for grim
